{
  "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
  "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 09-1036, Henderson v. Shinseki. Ms. Blatt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Lisa S. Blatt (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Federal Circuit's decision in this case forecloses judicial review when the very disability for which a veteran seeks benefits prevents the veteran from filing a timely appeal with the Veterans Court. That decision is wrong, and for three reasons the court of appeals erred in holding that the deadline at issue in this case is jurisdictional."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: And that is jurisdictional, 7292?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government's position assumes that no matter what the circumstances were -- and remember, a lot of these cases, the veteran is actually timely filing his appeal; he mistakenly files in the Veterans Administration rather than the Veterans Court. And the Government's position assumes that these uncounseled veterans are simply out of time and out of luck with no exception."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Veterans' organizations (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the veterans' organizations that filed amicus briefs say they also make the same mistake. They're not lawyers, and they often file in the wrong forum, too."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Lisa S. Blatt (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, he's out of luck, according to the Government. That's just tough."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Blatt, are you -- are you -- we have in Bowles itself -- it was from the district court to the court of appeals, and then we have from the court of appeals to this Court. Those two"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So whenever we have time limits in the future that do not contain any -- any explicit provision for waiver of failure to meet those time limits, you're asking us to find that all of those are non-jurisdictional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All statute of limitations are not jurisdictional. So there's no question -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF ERIC D. MILLER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What happens if the -- if the notice of decision is mistakenly mailed to the wrong address, comes back undeliverable, and no further notice is sent? Your -- you position is, once the 120 days expires, the veteran is out of luck?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In what percentage of the cases is there a representative?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: And you say -- you say that 80 percent of the time there is a registered -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MILLER: There -- there is a procedure for official accreditation of representatives -\u00ad CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERT: Right. MR. MILLER: -- from organizations like the American Legion, and if that person is registered as the claimant's representative in the proceeding before the board, then they would get a copy of the notice under 7104."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But what happened in this case? Was there -- was there a registered representative?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0003-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Counsel",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "04c3be04cdca284a445bbf03ab69652655ec153833940a6c8947d97c0b2b754f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c3be04cdca-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "don't even -- the Government doesn't even contest these because it has to be based on the record before, and all we're talking about is an extra 30 days or 60 days."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1036",
